      "id": "pbps-actual-hazard-clock",
      "library": "pbps",
      "chapter": "pbps-01",
      "chapter_path": "example-cases/samplewiki/companions/proximal-bouncy-particle.html",
      "title": "Actual PBPS integrated hazard and first exponential clock",
      "source": {
        "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2609.06905v1#A1",
        "edition": "arXiv2609.06905v1",
        "anchor": "arXiv2609.06905v1 Algorithm1, Proposition3.1, AppendixA.1 equation(A.1), Ex1-8; one-segment prerequisites for recursive equation(A.2).",
        "wording_status": "faithful paraphrase",
        "attribution": "Fan Chen, Sinho Chewi, Jianfeng Lu and Matthew S. Zhang, arXiv:2609.06905v1, Algorithm1 and AppendixA.1 equation(A.1), Ex1–8. ASTIS supplies omitted continuous-first-crossing and measure details. Recursive equation(A.2) and the full Proposition3.1 stochastic construction remain later consumers."
      },
      "statement": "Let E be a finite-dimensional real inner-product Borel space, including rank zero. Let V:E→ℝ be C², let α,β≥0 satisfy 0<α≤β and α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for all x,v, and let η>0 with βη≤1. For arbitrary y,xRef and z=(x,p), define c=y−η∇V(xRef), Φ_t(z)=(c+cos(t)(x−c)+√η sin(t)p, −sin(t)(x−c)/√η+cos(t)p), λ(xRef,(u,q))=√η max(0,⟨q,∇V(u)−∇V(xRef)⟩), H(z)=(η⁻¹‖x−c‖²+‖p‖²)/2, and C(z)=√η β√(2H(z))(√(2ηH(z))+‖c−xRef‖). For t≥0 put Λ_z(t)=∫₀ᵗλ(xRef,Φ_s(z))ds and τ_z(e)=inf{t≥0:Λ_z(t)≥e}, returning ∞ when this set is empty. Let W_z be the pushforward of Exp(1) on ℝ by e↦τ_z(max(e,0)). Then: (1) Λ is jointly continuous in y,xRef,z,t; (2) Λ is jointly Borel; (3) the actual orbit rate is integrable on every finite [0,t]; (4) Λ_z(0)=0, Λ_z(t)≥0 and Λ_z is nondecreasing; (5) for every e,t≥0, τ_z(e)≤t iff e≤Λ_z(t); (6) τ_z(e)=∞ iff Λ_z(t)<e for every finite t, finite τ_z(e) satisfies Λ_z(τ_z(e))=e, e>0 implies τ_z(e)>0, and τ_z(0)=0; (7) τ is jointly Borel in y,xRef,z,e; (8) W_z is a probability measure on [0,∞] and W_z((t,∞])=exp(−Λ_z(t)) for every finite t; (9) C(z)≥0 and Λ_z(t)≤C(z)t; (10) C(z)>0 implies max(e/C(z),0)≤τ_z(e), while C(z)=0 and e>0 imply τ_z(e)=∞. Every conclusion is derived for the actual flow and rate using their compiled laws. No unbounded-hazard or almost-sure finite-wait assumption is made. This is one flow-segment clock law used by AppendixA.1(A.1) and the future recursion(A.2). Recursive paths, nonexplosion, Markov memorylessness, invariance, terminal sampling kernels, main bounds and query costs remain open.",
      "assumptions": [
        "E is a finite-dimensional real inner-product space with its compatible norm and Borel measurable structure; product spaces use product structures. Rank zero is allowed.",
        "V:E→ℝ is C² on all E. The nonnegative α,β satisfy 0<α and α≤β, and α‖v‖²≤D²V(x)[v,v]≤β‖v‖² for every x,v∈E.",
        "η is real, η>0 and βη≤1. These are exactly the six original analytic callers. Flow/rate continuity, integrability, hazard monotonicity, an arbitrary cap, positivity of energy and finiteness of a random wait are never supplied as callers.",
        "All y,xRef∈E, initial phase z=(x,p)∈E×E, continuous nonnegative times t and thresholds e≥0 are arbitrary. The eight c,Φ,λ,H,C,Λ,τ,W definitions below are the literal definitions.",
        "τ takes values in [0,∞], with τ=∞ when no finite cumulative-hazard crossing exists. e=0 is included and gives τ=0. The finite-hitting identity has an explicit τ≠∞ guard.",
        "W is the actual pushforward of the unit-rate real exponential measure under e↦τ(toNNReal e); its measurability and probability normalization are conclusions. The waiting lower bound assumes C>0 only in its own implication; the C=0,e>0 branch gives τ=∞."
      ],
      "formulae": [
        {
          "label": "Actual harmonic orbit",
          "tex": "c=y-\\eta\\nabla V(x_{\\rm ref}),\\quad\\Phi_t(x,p)=\\bigl(c+\\cos t(x-c)+\\sqrt\\eta\\sin t\\,p,-\\tfrac{\\sin t}{\\sqrt\\eta}(x-c)+\\cos t\\,p\\bigr)."
        },
        {
          "label": "Actual rate, energy and majorant",
          "tex": "\\lambda(x_{\\rm ref},(x,p))=\\sqrt\\eta\\max\\{0,\\langle p,\\nabla V(x)-\\nabla V(x_{\\rm ref})\\rangle\\},\\quad H(z)=\\tfrac12(\\eta^{-1}\\|x-c\\|^2+\\|p\\|^2),\\quad C(z)=\\sqrt\\eta\\,\\beta\\sqrt{2H(z)}\\bigl(\\sqrt{2\\eta H(z)}+\\|c-x_{\\rm ref}\\|\\bigr)."
        },
        {
          "label": "Continuous cumulative hazard and first crossing",
          "tex": "\\Lambda_z(t)=\\int_0^t\\lambda(x_{\\rm ref},\\Phi_s z)\\,ds,\\quad\\tau_z(e)=\\inf\\{t\\ge0:\\Lambda_z(t)\\ge e\\}\\in[0,\\infty],\\quad\\inf\\varnothing=\\infty."
        },
        {
          "label": "Actual exponential law and waiting bound",
          "tex": "W_z=(e\\mapsto\\tau_z(\\max\\{e,0\\}))_\\#\\operatorname{Exp}(1),\\quad W_z((t,\\infty])=e^{-\\Lambda_z(t)},\\quad\\Lambda_z(t)\\le C(z)t,\\quad\\tau_z(e)\\ge e/C(z)\\ (C(z)>0)."
        }
      ],
